ask(c,'What does [a2,a3]=np.linalg.solve(A,B) do for this 2×2 system?', ['Solve A·[a2,a3]ᵀ=B and unpack the two coefficients','Multiply A and B elementwise and unpack two rows','Explicitly calculate the inverse matrix and assign it to both coefficients','Solve B·[a2,a3]ᵀ=A'], ['The call solves the linear coefficient system and returns its two unknowns.','Elementwise multiplication is not a linear-system solve.','The returned object is a solution vector, not the inverse matrix.','A is the coefficient matrix and B the right-hand side.'],kind='code_output',steps=['Read the matrix columns as coefficients of a2 and a3.','Solve for the length-two vector, then assign its first and second entries.'])
ask(c,'For the printed A=[[T²,T³],[2T,3T²]], what is det(A), and when is this coefficient solve nonsingular?', ['T⁴, so it is nonsingular for T>0','5T⁴, so it is singular for every positive T','T³, so it is nonsingular only when T=1','0, because both rows involve T'], ['The determinant is 3T⁴−2T⁴=T⁴, nonzero for positive duration.','The determinant uses subtraction, not addition; positive T does not make it singular.','The products both have fourth power.','Shared use of a variable does not imply proportional rows.'],kind='numerical',difficulty='medium',steps=['Use ad−bc for a 2×2 matrix.','T²·3T²−T³·2T=3T⁴−2T⁴=T⁴.','Positive T gives a nonzero determinant.'],formula=[fm('det(A)=T⁴',{'A':'2×2 cubic endpoint coefficient matrix [[T²,T³],[2T,3T²]]','T':'duration'},{'T':'s','det(A)':'s⁴'},['The first row is a position equation and the second a velocity equation; the determinant’s time power follows their coefficient products.'])])
ask(c,'If tf is changed to zero while the 10°→70° endpoint positions remain, what happens to the printed linear solve?', ['A becomes singular, and np.linalg.solve raises a linear-algebra error','The call automatically chooses an infinite velocity and returns valid coefficients','The call silently changes theta_f to theta_0','The call returns the original five-second coefficients unchanged'], ['Both rows of A become zero, so no solution can satisfy the nonzero position residual.','The library does not replace the singular system with an infinite-rate trajectory.','The input endpoints are not changed by solve.','Changing the matrix changes the problem.'],kind='code_output',difficulty='medium',steps=['With tf=0, A is the 2×2 zero matrix.','B remains [60,0], so the first equation is impossible.','NumPy reports a singular matrix rather than returning a valid cubic.'],assumptions=['The imports and other printed inputs remain unchanged.'])
ask(c,'Why does the code use theta_f−a0−a1*tf, rather than theta_f−a0 alone, in B?', ['It subtracts the known initial-velocity contribution from the final-position equation','It converts theta_f from degrees to radians','It forces a1 to zero even when a nonzero value was supplied','It approximates a second derivative numerically'], ['The known a1tf term belongs on the other side before solving for a2 and a3.','No angle conversion is performed.','a1 remains the supplied initial velocity.','This is algebraic elimination, not finite differencing.'],kind='code_output',difficulty='medium',steps=['Start from theta_f=a0+a1tf+a2tf²+a3tf³.','Move a0 and a1tf to the right-hand side.'])
ask(c,'What does t=np.linspace(0,5,100) produce in the source program?', ['100 evenly spaced samples including 0 and 5, with spacing 5/99 s','100 samples excluding 5, with spacing 5/100 s','101 samples including 0 and 5, with spacing 5/100 s','Five samples with spacing 100 s'], ['The default endpoint inclusion yields 99 intervals between 100 samples.','Endpoint exclusion would require a different option.','The third argument is the sample count, not interval count.','The argument roles are start, stop and sample count.'],kind='code_output',steps=['Read num=100 and the default endpoint=True.','The count of equal intervals is 100−1=99.','Spacing is (5−0)/99 seconds.'])
