ask(c,'The summary says cubic interpolation has continuous acceleration. Which interpretation is correct for a piecewise trajectory?', ['Acceleration is continuous within each cubic segment; C2 at joins additionally requires matching endpoint accelerations','Any two cubic segments automatically have matching acceleration','A cubic’s acceleration is discontinuous at every interior point','Continuous endpoint velocity implies matching endpoint acceleration'], ['Each polynomial is smooth internally, but independently chosen segments may have different second derivatives at a join.','Degree alone does not impose cross-segment equality.','A cubic has linear, hence continuous, interior acceleration.','Matching a first derivative does not force matching its derivative.'],difficulty='medium',pages=[502,486],conflict=(502,'Cubic interpolation ensures continuity of position, velocity, and acceleration.','A single cubic is smooth. For multiple segments, matching position and velocity only establishes C1; additional acceleration constraints are needed for C2.'))
