ask(c,'Does choosing quintic segments alone guarantee the summary’s “C2 continuity across segments”?', ['No; adjacent endpoint position, velocity and acceleration values must agree','Yes; degree five overrides any mismatched endpoint positions','Yes; quintics cannot have nonzero endpoint accelerations','No; quintics can never achieve C2 across a join'], ['The six boundary conditions permit acceleration control, but their assigned values must be compatible across the join.','Different endpoint positions would even break C0.','Quintic boundary data can prescribe nonzero accelerations.','Properly matched quintics can achieve C2.'],difficulty='medium',pages=[493,502],conflict=(502,'Quintic interpolation achieves C2 continuity across segments.','The degree supplies enough coefficients to specify endpoint accelerations; C2 follows only if neighboring position, velocity and acceleration boundary values match.'))
